      <Docs>
        <summary>Gets the registration expiry value supplied to the constructor.</summary>
        <value>The supplied expiry value, unchanged.</value>
        <remarks>
          <para>The .NET event data class does not convert this value to a duration or a timestamp. Android's listener documentation describes <c>expiryTime</c> as a duration in seconds. However, the Android 11 listener relay adds <c>System.currentTimeMillis()</c> to a positive registration duration without converting that duration. Do not assume that values from this relay are a count of seconds or a correctly scaled expiry timestamp.</para>
          <para>See the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/opt/net/voip/+/refs/tags/android-11.0.0_r1/src/java/android/net/sip/SipRegistrationListener.java">Android listener contract</a></format> and the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/opt/net/voip/+/refs/tags/android-11.0.0_r1/src/java/android/net/sip/SipManager.java">Android 11 listener relay</a></format>.</para>
          <para>Portions of this page are modifications based on work created and shared by the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/site-policies" title="Android Open Source Project">Android Open Source Project</a></format> and used according to terms described in the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5/" title="Creative Commons 2.5 Attribution License">Creative Commons 2.5 Attribution License.</a></format></para>
